{:edb/db-before-t 1493 :edb/db-after-t 1494 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534806 50 #inst "2026-10-12T15:29:06.960Z" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186096665 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436667 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186096665 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436670 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186096666 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436669 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186096668 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436668 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186096847 1050 1380.0 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186097508 1061 1696 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186097508 1061 637993 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186097509 1061 1697 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186097509 1061 637994 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186097510 1061 1700 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186097510 1061 637997 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186097511 1061 1701 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186097511 1061 638001 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186097512 1061 1703 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186097512 1061 638004 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186097513 1061 1705 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186097513 1061 637998 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186097922 1064 "How can we calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x?$ \n\nNotice that we have the product of sine and cosine with the same argument $(x).$ In such cases, we can use the double-angle formula for sine to solve the integral.\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for sine, which is\n\n$$\n\\sin {2x}=2\\sin x \\cos x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\sin x \\cos x =  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin {2x}.\n$$\n\nPlugging this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {2x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{4} \\cos {2x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nIn general, we can use the double-angle formula for sine to solve any integral that's of the form \n\n$$\n\\int \\sin\\left(ax+b\\right)\\cos(ax+b)\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n Let's take a look at another example." 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186097922 1064 "How can we calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x?$  \n\nNotice that we have the product of sine and cosine with the same argument $(x).$ In such cases, we can use the double-angle formula for sine to solve the integral.\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for sine, which is\n\n$$\n\\sin {2x}=2\\sin x \\cos x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\sin x \\cos x =  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin {2x}.\n$$\n\nPlugging this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {2x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{4} \\cos {2x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nIn general, we can use the double-angle formula for sine to solve any integral that's of the form \n\n$$\n\\int \\sin\\left(ax+b\\right)\\cos(ax+b)\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n Let's take a look at another example." 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186097923 1064 "Let's recall the three double-angle formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}(2x) & ={cos}^{2}x-{sin}^{2}x \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}x-1 \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the double-angle formulas for cosine to integrate $\\sin^2{x}$ and $\\cos^2{x}.$ Let's take a look at some examples." 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186097923 1064 "Let's recall the three double-angle formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the double-angle formulas for cosine to integrate $\\sin^2{x}$ and $\\cos^2{x}.$ Let's take a look at some examples." 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186318511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436651 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186318511 1078 #edb/ref 17592186318158 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186318511 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436651 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186318549 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436650 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186318549 1078 #edb/ref 17592186318102 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186318549 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436650 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186318595 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436656 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186318595 1078 #edb/ref 17592186317895 13194139534806 17592186045417 false] [17592186318595 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436656 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436648 1080 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436648 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436648 1083 #uuid "0f0f1116-d915-5ec7-81c7-f4086a52153e" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436649 1080 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+C" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436649 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436649 1083 #uuid "117955a3-da81-5764-9c65-84ef3f86d82f" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436650 1080 "-2\\pi" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436650 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436650 1083 #uuid "140301e9-e5d7-5ea2-aa4c-0f869d4dbf85" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436651 1080 "3\\pi" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436651 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436651