ame{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436668 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436666 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436668 1069 "q-10558" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436668 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436668 1071 "$\\int (x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x+{cos}^{2}⁡3x)\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436668 1072 #uuid "63aa6d59-1b3d-5a26-a1f9-94507bee325e" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436668 1074 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x+{cos}^{2}⁡3x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (x+{cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436669 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436664 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436669 1069 "q-361712" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436669 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436669 1071 "![](images/a7/a71e9121e38cfa60bfac0864ee2686cad756e268b78b512f55367bf6af0f8c94.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436669 1072 #uuid "bfe0bdd7-dbe2-5dd0-8dfa-8c8cabd2a658" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436669 1074 "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x))\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x) & =3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+({sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\frac{5}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5}{2}x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}]-[\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot 0)+\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 0] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{5\\pi }{8}]-[\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot 0+\\frac{5\\pi }{8}]-[\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot 0+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436670 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436665 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436670 1069 "q-114680" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436670 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436670 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436670 1072 #uuid "f11e7aad-252b-5e12-b641-681cfb746b6c" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true] [17592186436670 1074 "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-[0-1] \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534806 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0f0f1116-d915-5ec7-81c7-f4086a52153e" 17592186436648 "answer-117955a3-da81-5764-9c65-84ef3f86d82f" 17592186436649 "answer-140301e9-e5d7-5ea2-aa4c-0f869d4dbf85" 175921864366